{
  "id": "4168ad4c-9ee7-5180-91fd-7a9c63af3ee1",
  "quality_score": 0.72,
  "review_status": "auto-approved",
  "content_json": {
    "id": "tr-b1-past-continuous-iyordu",
    "cefr": "B1",
    "title": "Past continuous -(I)yordu",
    "sections": [
      {
        "id": "what-is-it",
        "body": [
          {
            "kind": "paragraph",
            "text": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "The past continuous is formed by combining the present-continuous suffix "
              },
              {
                "kind": "hilite",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "-(I)yor"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " with the past copular suffix "
              },
              {
                "kind": "hilite",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "-DI"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " plus a personal ending. The result expresses an action or state that was in progress at a specific moment in the past ("
              },
              {
                "kind": "em",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "was/were …ing"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "), or a repeated action that was typical of a past period ("
              },
              {
                "kind": "em",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "used to …"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "). It is the direct past-tense counterpart of the present continuous: wherever "
              },
              {
                "kind": "mono",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "geliyor"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " describes something happening now, "
              },
              {
                "kind": "mono",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "geliyordu"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " places that same ongoing action in the past."
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "title": "what is it?"
      },
      {
        "id": "when-to-use-it",
        "body": [
          {
            "kind": "list",
            "items": [
              [
                {
                  "kind": "paragraph",
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "kind": "strong",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "Action in progress at a past moment."
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " Use -(I)yordu when one action was already underway when something else happened, or when you are describing the background scene of a past narrative. English equivalent: «was/were …ing»."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "paragraph",
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "kind": "strong",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "Habitual or repeated action in the past."
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " Use -(I)yordu for something that happened regularly over a past period but no longer does. English equivalent: «used to …» or «would …» (in a narrative sense)."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "paragraph",
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "kind": "strong",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "Past states."
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " Stative verbs (knowing, understanding, wanting, etc.) that describe a condition rather than an event also take -(I)yordu to express that the state held over a past period."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            ]
          }
        ],
        "title": "when to use it"
      },
      {
        "id": "formation",
        "body": [
          {
            "kind": "paragraph",
            "text": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "The suffix chain is: "
              },
              {
                "kind": "strong",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "verb stem + -(I)yor + -du/dü/tu/tü + personal ending"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": ". Three rules govern the shape of each part."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "kind": "list",
            "items": [
              [
                {
                  "kind": "paragraph",
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "kind": "strong",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "-(I)yor buffer vowel."
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " If the stem ends in a consonant, a buffer vowel is inserted before "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "-yor"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": ": "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "ı/i/u/ü"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " according to four-way vowel harmony with the stem's last vowel. If the stem ends in a vowel, that vowel drops and "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "-yor"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " attaches directly (e.g. "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "bekle- → bekliyor"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": ")."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "paragraph",
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "kind": "strong",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "-DI consonant mutation."
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " The "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "D"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " of the past copula is always "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "d"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " here because "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "-yor"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " ends in the voiced consonant "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "r"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": ". The vowel of -DI follows two-way back/front harmony with the stem's last vowel: "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "-du"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " (back rounded), "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "-dü"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " (front rounded), "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "-du"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " (back unrounded → also "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "du"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": "), "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "-di"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " (front unrounded). In practice the vowel of -(I)yor is always "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "o"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": ", so the copula vowel harmonises with the stem, not with "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "o"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": "."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "paragraph",
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "kind": "strong",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "Personal endings."
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " The endings after -DI are the same set used in the simple past tense: "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "-m, -n, ∅, -k, -nız/niz/nuz/nüz, -lar/ler"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": "."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            ]
          },
          {
            "kind": "paragraph",
            "text": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "Full conjugation of "
              },
              {
                "kind": "mono",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "gel-"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " (to come) and "
              },
              {
                "kind": "mono",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "gör-"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " (to see):"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "head": [
              "person",
              "gel- (to come)",
              "gör- (to see)"
            ],
            "kind": "conjugation-table",
            "rows": [
              [
                "ben (I)",
                "geliyordum",
                "görüyordum"
              ],
              [
                "sen (you, sg.)",
                "geliyordun",
                "görüyordun"
              ],
              [
                "o (he/she/it)",
                "geliyordu",
                "görüyordu"
              ],
              [
                "biz (we)",
                "geliyorduk",
                "görüyorduk"
              ],
              [
                "siz (you, pl./formal)",
                "geliyordunuz",
                "görüyordunuz"
              ],
              [
                "onlar (they)",
                "geliyorlardı",
                "görüyorlardı"
              ]
            ]
          },
          {
            "kind": "callout",
            "variant": "default",
            "children": [
              {
                "kind": "paragraph",
                "text": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "The third-person plural "
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "mono",
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "text": "onlar"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": " form places the plural marker "
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "mono",
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "text": "-lar/-ler"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": " before the past copula: "
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "mono",
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "text": "geliyorlardı"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": ", not "
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "mono",
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "text": "*geliyordular"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": " (though the latter is heard in informal speech)."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "title": "formation"
      },
      {
        "id": "examples-in-context",
        "body": [
          {
            "en": "I was coming home.",
            "kind": "example",
            "note": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "Action in progress at a past moment. Stem "
              },
              {
                "kind": "mono",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "gel-"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " + "
              },
              {
                "kind": "mono",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "-iyor"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " + "
              },
              {
                "kind": "mono",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "-du"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " + "
              },
              {
                "kind": "mono",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "-m"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "."
              }
            ],
            "target": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "Eve "
              },
              {
                "kind": "hilite",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "geliyordum"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "en": "He used to get up early every morning.",
            "kind": "example",
            "note": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "Habitual past. The back vowel in "
              },
              {
                "kind": "mono",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "kalk-"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " triggers buffer "
              },
              {
                "kind": "mono",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "-ı-"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " and copula "
              },
              {
                "kind": "mono",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "-du"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "."
              }
            ],
            "target": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "Her sabah erken "
              },
              {
                "kind": "hilite",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "kalkıyordu"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "en": "We were eating.",
            "kind": "example",
            "note": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "Stem "
              },
              {
                "kind": "mono",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "ye-"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " loses its final vowel before "
              },
              {
                "kind": "mono",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "-yor"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": ", giving "
              },
              {
                "kind": "mono",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "yiyor-"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "; first-person plural ending "
              },
              {
                "kind": "mono",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "-k"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "."
              }
            ],
            "target": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "Biz yemek "
              },
              {
                "kind": "hilite",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "yiyorduk"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "en": "You knew Ömer better than me.",
            "kind": "example",
            "note": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "Stative use: "
              },
              {
                "kind": "mono",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "tanı-"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " (to know/recognise) describes a state, not an event. The stem ends in a vowel, so no buffer vowel is inserted."
              }
            ],
            "target": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "Sen Ömer'i benden iyi "
              },
              {
                "kind": "hilite",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "tanıyordun"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "."
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "title": "examples in context"
      },
      {
        "id": "common-pitfalls",
        "body": [
          {
            "kind": "list",
            "items": [
              [
                {
                  "kind": "paragraph",
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "kind": "strong",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "Using simple past -DI instead of -(I)yordu."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "kind": "paragraph",
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "Geldim"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " means «I came» — a completed event. "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "Geliyordum"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " means «I was coming» — an action in progress. Choosing the wrong form changes the meaning entirely. Ask yourself: was the action completed and bounded, or was it ongoing/habitual?"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "paragraph",
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "kind": "strong",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "Wrong vowel harmony on the -DI copula."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "kind": "paragraph",
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": "The copula vowel harmonises with the "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "strong",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "verb stem"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": ", not with the "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "o"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " in "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "-yor"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": ". "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "gel-"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " has a front vowel, so the copula is "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "-du"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " — giving "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "geliyordum"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": ", not "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "*geliyordüm"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": ". Check the stem's last vowel, not the suffix immediately before -DI."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "paragraph",
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "kind": "strong",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "Stacking two past markers."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "kind": "paragraph",
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": "A form like "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "*geldiyordum"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " — combining the simple past "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "-di"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " with the present continuous "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "-yor"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " — does not exist in Turkish. The past meaning comes entirely from the copular "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "-du/-dü"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " added after "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "-yor"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": ". Never insert a past suffix into the stem before "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "-yor"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": "."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            ]
          }
        ],
        "title": "common pitfalls"
      }
    ],
    "subtitle": "Describing ongoing or habitual actions in the past"
  }
}